<kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2">
  <Document>
    <name>🌊 LIVE WATER CLARITY / TURBIDITY</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<h2>LIVE WATER CLARITY / TURBIDITY</h2><p><b>Gradient key</b><br><img src="https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/water_clarity/legend.png" width="600" alt="gradient key"><br>Diffuse attenuation coefficient for PAR (m^-1), FIXED log-spaced scale <b>LOWEST 0.02</b> clearest (dark blue) → 0.1 → 0.3 → <b>1.0</b> turbid (red) → <b>HIGHEST+ 5+</b> most turbid (violet). Larger values always mean murkier water; source values are never altered.</p><p>This entry auto-refreshes from the live overlay (source: NOAA CoastWatch S-NPP VIIRS Kd(PAR) diffuse attenuation, Science Quality, Global 4 km, Daily (ERDDAP nesdisVHNSQkdparDaily), legacy NRT id as fallback).<br/><b>Data time:</b> 2026-09-15 08:00 AM EDT (newest of 7-day mosaic)<br/><b>Source version:</b> nesdisVHNSQkdparDaily-v3-2026-09-15<br/><b>Status:</b> LATEST AVAILABLE (daily composite)</p><p>Turn on/off independently of all other layers. Add this file once; new source cycles appear automatically.</p><p><i>Not endorsed by NOAA.</i></p>]]></description>
